{"id":"cual","es":"cuál","en":"which one","sv":"vilken","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"]},
{"id":"cuando","es":"cuándo","en":"when","sv":"när","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"Cuándo with the accent asks when. Without it, cuando links two events (cuando llegue, te llamo) — the accent is the only difference."},
{"id":"donde","es":"dónde","en":"where","sv":"var","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"]},
{"id":"como-pregunta","es":"cómo","en":"how","sv":"hur","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"Cómo with the accent asks how. Without it, como means as or like — and como is also I eat."},
