{"id":"porque","es":"porque","en":"because","sv":"eftersom, för att","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"One word, no accent. Written as two words with an accent — por qué — it asks why."},
{"id":"si","es":"si","en":"if","sv":"om","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"No accent: it means if. With an accent, sí means yes — the accent is the only difference."},
{"id":"cuando-conector","es":"cuando","en":"when (linking two events)","sv":"när (binder ihop två satser)","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"No accent: it links two events (cuando llegue, te llamo). With an accent, cuándo asks when."},
{"id":"sino","es":"sino","en":"but rather, but instead","sv":"utan","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"Follows a negative to correct it: no es rojo, sino azul — not red, but blue. Pero would sound odd there."},
{"id":"que-conector","es":"que","en":"that, which","sv":"att, som","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"No accent: it links a clause (creo que sí). With an accent, qué asks what."},
{"id":"aunque","es":"aunque","en":"although, even though","sv":"fastän, även om","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"]},
{"id":"entonces","es":"entonces","en":"then, so","sv":"då, alltså","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"]},
