{"id":"tampoco","es":"tampoco","en":"neither, not either","sv":"inte heller","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"Answers a negative statement: no puedo — yo tampoco, I can't — me neither (literally, not either)."},
{"id":"ademas","es":"además","en":"besides, furthermore","sv":"dessutom","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"]},
{"id":"pues","es":"pues","en":"well, so (filler word)","sv":"tja (utfyllnadsord)","pos":"other","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"A conversational filler that opens or hedges a sentence (pues, no sé — well, I don't know), lighter than entonces, which marks an actual consequence."},
{"id":"mucho","es":"mucho","en":"a lot of, much (with a noun or verb)","sv":"mycket (med substantiv eller verb)","pos":"adjective","track":"words","level":1,"themes":["conectores"],"note":"Goes with a noun (mucho tiempo, a lot of time) or a verb (trabaja mucho, he works a lot). Before an adjective, use muy instead."},
